                <head>253. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Prime Minister Harold Macmillan visited Athens August 7–9 for talks with
                    Karamanlis and Averoff on the future of Cyprus. Macmillan then flew to Ankara
                    where he met with Menderes and Zorlu on August 9 and 10 for further discussions
                    on Cyprus. On August 11, Macmillan flew to Cyprus to meet with British
                    administrators and representatives of the Greek and Turkish communities. For the
                    Prime Minister’s account of these meetings, see Riding the Storm, pages
                    674–683.</p>
            </div>
